Three CSS-only fixes to `modes/Hexium/Hexium.css` improving layout correctness on long words and small screens.

## Word Builder Strip — always single line
- `flex-wrap: wrap` → `flex-wrap: nowrap` + `overflow-x: auto`
- Scrollbar hidden visually (`scrollbar-width: none` / `::-webkit-scrollbar`) but remains functional
- No font or badge size reduction

## Filled Daily Slot — word fills the row
Extends `.daily-slot-row.is-filled .sub-word` to spread the revealed word across the full row width:
```css
.daily-slot-row.is-filled .sub-word {
  color: var(--accent);
  width: 100%;
  display: block;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 1.3rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  line-height: 1;
}
```

## Responsive Breakpoints — 2-tier → 3-tier
Replaces the non-standard `700px`/`400px` breakpoints with:

| Breakpoint | Target | `--hex-size` |
|---|---|---|
| `768px` | Tablet / large phone | `38px` |
| `480px` | Medium phone | `34px` (+ tighter gaps, panel padding, list height) |
| `360px` | Small / compact phone | `28px` |

