Please make the following three CSS changes to `modes/Hexium/Hexium.css`:

---

## 1. Word Builder Strip — always single line, no shrinking

The `.word-builder-strip` currently has `flex-wrap: wrap`, which causes long words (like "FORMICARIUM") to wrap onto a second row in the Current Word panel. Change it so the strip **never wraps** and instead scrolls horizontally if the word is very long. Do **not** reduce font size or badge size to compensate.

**Change:**
```css
/* BEFORE */
.word-builder-strip {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 6px;
  min-height: 44px;
  align-items: center;
}

/* AFTER */
.word-builder-strip {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: nowrap;
  gap: 6px;
  min-height: 44px;
  align-items: center;
  overflow-x: auto;
  /* hide scrollbar visually but keep it functional */
  scrollbar-width: none;
}
.word-builder-strip::-webkit-scrollbar {
  display: none;
}
```

---

## 2. Filled Daily Slot Rows — word fills the full row

When a daily slot is filled (`.daily-slot-row.is-filled`), the revealed word currently sits at the left at normal size. Instead, it should visually **fill the full row width** — use a larger font size, full width, centered, and expanded letter-spacing so it stretches across the available space. Do NOT overflow or truncate.

Currently the only rule for this is:
```css
.daily-slot-row.is-filled .sub-word {
  color: var(--accent);
}
```

**Change it to:**
```css
.daily-slot-row.is-filled .sub-word {
  color: var(--accent);
  width: 100%;
  display: block;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 1.3rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  line-height: 1;
}
```

---

## 3. Better Responsive Breakpoints

The current breakpoints are `max-width: 700px` and `max-width: 400px`. Update them to a more standard 3-tier system:

- **`768px`** — tablet portrait / large phone: switch to single-column layout (replaces current `700px`)
- **`480px`** — medium phone: slightly smaller hex tiles (`--hex-size: 34px`) and tighter panel gaps
- **`360px`** — small phone / compact mobile: smallest hex tiles (`--hex-size: 28px`) (replaces current `400px`)

**Replace the entire mobile responsive section** (currently at the bottom of Hexium.css before the `prefers-reduced-motion` block) with:

```css
